-- title:
--   varpi generates the maximal ideal at minimal primes of (varpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a principal ideal domain with fraction field $K_0$, let $F$ be a field equipped with compatible $R$- and $K_0$-algebra structures, and let $j \in F$ be a nonzero element that is transcendental over $R$ and such that $F$ is a finite separable extension of the intermediate field $K_0(j) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K₀ {j}`. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin R F j` for the subalgebra of $F$ consisting of all elements integral over $R[j] =$ `Algebra.adjoin R {j}`, i.e. the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$. Let $\varpi \in R$ be a prime element. Assume the following multiplicity-one condition on valuation subrings: for every valuation subring $V \subseteq F$ such that the image of $R$ lies in $V$, such that the image of $\varpi$ in $F$ is a nonunit of $V$, and such that for every polynomial $P \in R[X]$ not divisible by $\varpi$ (as a constant polynomial) both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$, every nonunit $x$ of $V$ satisfies $x \varpi^{-1} \in V$. Then for every prime ideal $\mathfrak p$ of $A$ that is a minimal prime over the ideal of $A$ generated by the image of $\varpi$, the image of that ideal under the localisation map $A \to A_{\mathfrak p}$ is the maximal ideal of $A_{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   The statement converts a multiplicity-one hypothesis, formulated on the valuation subrings of $F$ that dominate $R$ with $\varpi$ a nonunit and that invert all polynomials in $j$ prime to $\varpi$, into the algebraic assertion that $\varpi$ generates the maximal ideal of the local ring of the $j$-finite chart at each minimal prime of $(\varpi)$; the chart ring is a Noetherian normal domain with fraction field $F$, so such a local ring is a discrete valuation ring. It serves as the valuation-theoretic input to the reducedness of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model, and is applied to the modular curve $X_H$ in [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.map_span_natCast_eq_maximalIdeal_of_mem_minimalPrimes_chartAlg_gammaH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.map_span_natCast_eq_maximalIdeal_of_mem_minimalPrimes_chartAlg_gammaH).
